assessments:
- assessment_id: cerium-form
  area: identity
  topic: P1/P2 exact supplied form and nonidentity grounding
  outcome: supported
  target_ids:
  - ORIGINAL-w02::c-proposal-cerium-nitrate-hexahydrate
  summary: The exact source transition preserves cerium(III) nitrate hexahydrate under
    cas:10294-41-4 with a broad-only parent mapping.
  evidence_ids:
  - semantics
  - payload-0
  - ce-source
  - ce-properties
  - ce-cas
  - ce-mesh
  - ce-stock
  details: The former raw queue spelling lacks the verified parentheses and stays
    REJECTED_LABEL. The correct provider spelling remains RAW_TEXT. PubChem properties
    match six waters; no parent identity, role, supplier procurement or subclass assertion
    is approved. M0319657 is a MeSH Concept; the payload word descriptor is not an
    assertion of its RDF class. All previous history and occurrence counts remain.
    This review supports the source promotion but does not supply a Cerium source-export
    binding.
- assessment_id: arabinan-alias
  area: nomenclature
  topic: P2/P3 botanical qualification and alias boundary
  outcome: supported
  target_ids:
  - ORIGINAL-w03::m-arabinan_source_alias
  summary: The sugar-beet-preserving RAW_TEXT alias and appended history are supported,
    with existing identity and broad mapping unchanged.
  evidence_ids:
  - semantics
  - payload-1
  - ara-source
  - ara-term
  - ara-recipe
  details: The full before/after comparison retains all other fields. Existing CAS11078-27-6
    is not evidence that P-ARAB and P-LARB grades are interchangeable. No exact generic-arabinan
    ontology replacement, procurement, purity or role is added. Historical no-exact-term
    notes are preserved history, not a new exhaustive ontology-absence claim.
- assessment_id: barley-input
  area: identity
  topic: P2/P3 original material and preparation stage
  outcome: supported
  target_ids:
  - ORIGINAL-w10::bio-proposal-Barley_Grains
  summary: Singular Barley grain is a supported raw source alias for the retained
    grain-input owner.
  evidence_ids:
  - payload-2
  - barley-source
  - barley-recipe
  - semantics
  details: Only the synonym/history delta is proposed. UNMAPPED_0096, UNMAPPED status,
    UNDEFINED_MIXTURE and occurrence statistics remain. A counted grain is not assigned
    a guessed mass, cultivar, species ontology, food ontology or role. The primary
    preparation adds grain before autoclaving; no identity with the processed medium
    is asserted. Future stable-ID adoption must independently preserve this owner
    and may support MIM-only output only under its own gates.
- assessment_id: estradiol-beta
  area: identity
  topic: P1/P2 stereochemistry and source quantity separation
  outcome: supported
  target_ids:
  - ORIGINAL-w10::chem-proposal-99
  summary: Creating the beta-specific chemical record at CHEBI16469 is supported while
    the quantity/source/export conflict stays held.
  evidence_ids:
  - payload-3
  - estradiol-source
  - estradiol-term
  - estradiol-recipe
  - semantics
  details: The exact source and canonical term agree on17beta identity and SYNONYM_MATCH
    semantics. The payload contains no imported dose or role. The1mg primary input
    and frozen1g/L value are not reconciled by this record. Agent-authored evidence
    remains LLM_SUGGESTION and the#1226 correction/history remains intact. This source
    review grants no source-binding or export acceptance.
findings: []
actions: []
limitations:
- This is the legacy LC source stage. No stable MIM ID has been assigned or applied
  by this review; actual TC adoption, rename/alias continuity and real export/consumer
  canary remain separate required outcomes.
- A source-transition finding-free review is not complete-payload publication approval.
  Preserved dose, supplier/procurement, role, source-binding and export holds remain;
  MEM is outside the four source-review targets and its hold is not cleared.
- Captured primary/ontology documents were inspected locally. No paid provider call,
  exhaustive ontology-absence search, new supplier attribution or approval of every
  depositor synonym was made.
- Native source-plan admission, guarded application, currentness and final release
  validation remain required after the distinct skeptical review. Passed dependency
  suites were not repeated for this report.
notes:
- MeSH M0319657 is treated as a Concept with a broad mapping, regardless of incidental
  descriptor wording in historical evidence text.
- P1-P4 rubric is preserved through per-target assessments; no numeric score is used
  as scientific or publication approval.
tags:
- canary
- source-transition
- primary
- scientific-review
- holds-preserved
